        "-600": "Gaul enters its La Tène period as Celtic culture reaches sophisticated heights, master craftsmen producing exquisite metalwork while druids preserve oral traditions encompassing law, astronomy, and theology, yet tribal divisions persist—Arverni, Aedui, Sequani among dozens of peoples whose shifting alliances and endemic warfare will eventually facilitate Roman conquest, though Greek colonists at Massalia introduce Mediterranean trade and literacy to southern Gaul.",
